// v3.compiler.parse_tables — SG-2c-1 grammar-tables prototype authority.
//
// **SG-2c cluster (structural lane) — `parse_primary` prefix + atom family.**
// Two table surfaces in one function: (A) `PrimaryPrefixRow` / `primary_prefix_dispatch`
// (SG-2c-6), (B) `PrimaryAtomRow` / `primary_atom_class` (SG-2c-7). Same-PR receipt:
// authority in this file; `regen_parse_tables` to `parse_tables_generated.rs`;
// `regen_parse` of `parse_parser_body.txt` to `parse_generated.rs`;
// `sg2c1_parse_tables_authority_test` ratchet; open-coded `TokenKind` dispatch in
// `parse_primary` removed in favor of those projections.
//
// **Scope.** SG-2c proper (parser authority proper — retiring
// `parse_parser_body.txt` as parse logic) is blocked on a named
// substrate capability: recursive list-body emission over `List<Token>`
// with cursor threading. See `src/v3/std/list.dag:13-15` ("the current
// compiler still lacks full structural recursion + list-body emission
// support") and SELF_HOSTING.md §6 Phase 4a. Until that lands, any full
// `.dag` parser port routes through a hidden Rust host layer, which
// SG-2c's STOP-AND-ESCALATE bullet forbids.
//
// **What this file is.** The bounded, honest subset of parser
// authority that DOES fit current `.dag` capabilities: pure
// declarative tables: (1) binary operator token-to-semantics mapping
// (SG-2c-1), (2) top-level item keyword → `parse_item` dispatch
// class (SG-2c-2), (3) type-RHS boundary keyword membership
// (SG-2c-3), (4) bracket opener/closer role membership (SG-2c-4,
// consumed by the parser's depth-tracking scan helpers `skip_where_clause`
// and `rhs_is_sum`), (5) primary-expression prefix openers (SG-2c-6,
// consumed by `parse_primary`), and (6) primary-expression atomic tail tokens
// after the prefix pass (SG-2c-7, same function). The binary-operator table replaced hand-coded
// matches across five parser precedence functions in
// `parse_parser_body.txt`
// (`parse_logical_or`, `parse_logical_and`, `parse_comparison`,
// `parse_additive`, `parse_term`). Those functions now call the
// generated helper `binary_op_at_level` instead of open-coding the
// token → `OperatorKind` match. **SG-2c cluster (prefix + atom family):** after
// the `parse_primary` prefix pass (`PrimaryPrefixRow` →
// `primary_prefix_dispatch`, SG-2c-6), the non-prefix first token of a primary
// is classified by `PrimaryAtomRow` (SG-2c-7) via `primary_atom_class` so the
// closed set of `Int`/`true`/`false`/string/lambda/ident forms stays table-owned.
//
// **What this file is NOT.** Parser control flow. Cursor mechanics.
// Error recovery. Item-kind dispatch. Recursive-descent itself. Those
// remain semantic authority in `parse_parser_body.txt` (explicitly
// residual; see header there).
//
// **Dissolution trigger.** Full parser authority proper (SG-2c
// proper) is blocked on recursive list-body emission from
// `std/list.dag`. Once that lands, `parse_parser_body.txt` can be
// ported to `.dag` as recursive-descent functions on `List<Token>`
// and this table becomes one data section of a larger `parse.dag`
// (or merges into a Phase 4b grammar-as-data spec).
//
// **Rust projection.** `src/v3/compiler/src/parse_tables_generated.rs`
// is produced by `cargo run -p v3-compiler --bin regen_parse_tables`
// — do not hand-edit it. The freshness ratchet lives in
// `tests/integration/sg2c1_parse_tables_authority_test.rs`.
//
// **Same-PR consumer (E-6).** SG-2c-2 projection `top_level_item_dispatch`
// / Rust `ItemDispatchKind` (derived from keyword rows only) is consumed by the
// live parser: `parse_item` in `parse_parser_body.txt` (spliced into
// `parse_generated.rs` via `regen_parse`).
//
// **Same-PR consumer (E-6).** SG-2c-3 projection `is_type_rhs_boundary_keyword`
// is emitted from the existing `TopLevelItemKwRow` facts and consumed by the
// live parser's type-RHS lookahead helpers `skip_where_clause` and
// `rhs_is_sum` in `parse_parser_body.txt`.
//
// **Same-PR consumer (E-6).** SG-2c-4 projection `bracket_role` / `BracketRole`
// is emitted from `BracketRow` facts and consumed by the same type-RHS
// helpers `skip_where_clause` and `rhs_is_sum` in `parse_parser_body.txt`,
// replacing two duplicated inline bracket-membership match blocks.
//
// **Same-PR consumer (E-6).** SG-2c-6 projection `primary_prefix_dispatch` /
// `PrimaryPrefixDispatch` is emitted from `PrimaryPrefixRow` facts and
// consumed by `parse_primary` in `parse_parser_body.txt`, replacing the
// four inline `if matches!(peek, …)` prefix probes.
//
// **Same-PR consumer (E-6).** SG-2c-7 projection `primary_atom_class` /
// `PrimaryAtomClass` is emitted from `PrimaryAtomRow` facts and consumed
// in the same `parse_primary` function after the prefix pass, replacing the
// open `match` on the post-bump `TokenKind` for atomic primary forms.

module v3.compiler.parse_tables

// Precedence level of a binary operator. Mirrors the five parser
// precedence functions in `parse_parser_body.txt` (lowest to highest
// binding): logical-or, logical-and, comparison, additive,
// multiplicative. The parser consumes this enum by filtering
// `binary_op_at_level(token, LEVEL)` at each precedence function.
//
// Dissolution classification: **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** per
// `docs/modeling-discipline.md` §4. A richer source exists
// (precedence is a 1D numeric ordering — Pattern 4), but
// extraction is not cheap today: a precedence-climbing surface
// grammar reformulation rides the same lane as SG-2c proper,
// which is blocked on recursive list-body emission over
// `List<Token>`. See trigger at the bottom of this ledger.
//
// Dissolution ledger (4-pattern check per THESIS §"Structural
// decompression"; MODELING M7 / feedback_coproduct_dissolution):
// - **Pattern 1 (fact placement)**: fails. Each variant is just a
//   coordinate key, not a distinct payload shape. Scattering into
//   five per-variant side tables ("is_or_level", "is_and_level", ...)
//   would duplicate `BinaryOpRow` per level with no payload
//   difference, adding dispatch rather than removing it.
// - **Pattern 2 (variant-is-data)**: fails. All variants are nullary
//   and structurally identical — this IS the discriminant-only shape;
//   a unified representation would be the enum itself.
// - **Pattern 3 (algebraic form)**: fails. There is no shared
//   algebra the five variants inhabit; they are distinct parser
//   control-flow points, not elements of a computed structure.
// - **Pattern 4 (dimensional)**: **passes structurally, deferred
//   on substrate**. Precedence is a 1D total order
//   (Or < And < Comparison < Additive < Multiplicative) and could
//   be encoded as `Int where 1 <= n <= 5`. Not extracted today
//   because (a) the only consumer is five hand-authored parser
//   functions in `parse_parser_body.txt` that select by name —
//   there is no algebraic consumer that exploits the dimension
//   yet, so collapsing to `Int` loses `binary_op_at_level`'s
//   exhaustive `match (tk, level)` without a corresponding gain;
//   (b) the consumer itself (the recursive-descent parser) is
//   pinned as residual semantic authority, blocked on the same
//   substrate gap as SG-2c proper.
//
// **Named trigger (YELLOW):** when surface-grammar precedence is
// reformulated as a structural fact — i.e. a precedence-climbing
// interpreter reading a numeric ordering — dissolve `BinaryOpLevel`
// to `Int where 1 <= n <= 5` and let the interpreter consume the
// dimension. That reformulation rides the same lane as SG-2c
// proper (retiring `parse_parser_body.txt`), which is blocked on
// recursive list-body emission over `List<Token>` per
// `src/v3/std/list.dag:13-15`. Both dissolutions unlock together.
type BinaryOpLevel
  = Or
  | And
  | Comparison
  | Additive
  | Multiplicative

// One row per binary-operator token. `token_variant` is the
// `TokenKind` variant name (e.g. "PipePipe"); `operator_symbol` is
// the canonical operator spelling that `operators.dag::from_symbol`
// already maps to an `OperatorKind`; `level` is the parser
// precedence function that should consume this token. Keyed on the
// textual variant name to avoid importing `tokenize.TokenKind` here
// (scope: declarative data only, not cross-module structural
// matching — that widens to SG-2c proper).
//
// **Grounding in the shared-syntax authority.** Each row is
// structurally cross-validated at regen time, so the table is a
// projection of the shared authority rather than a parallel
// restatement. Four joins close every drift surface:
// - `token_variant` must match a `TokenKind` variant in `tokenize.dag`
// - `operator_symbol` must map to an `OperatorKind` via
//   `operators.dag::from_symbol`
// - `(operator_symbol, level)` must agree with `dag_operators` in
//   `dsl/extdeps/languages/dag/syntax.dag`: the canonical
//   `left_bp` for the symbol must fall inside the bp band assigned
//   to the declared `level` (see `level_for_bp` in
//   `regen_parse_tables_emit.rs`)
// - the `OperatorKind` returned by `operators.dag::from_symbol` must
//   have a leaf variant whose name matches the shared authority's
//   `binop` field — so `operators.dag` and `dag_operators` cannot
//   disagree on what a symbol means
// If any shared authority shifts, regen fails closed here before
// any parser change ships.
type BinaryOpRow {
  token_variant: String
  operator_symbol: String
  level: BinaryOpLevel
}

data binary_op_pipepipe: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "PipePipe"
  operator_symbol: "||"
  level: Or
}

data binary_op_ampamp: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "AmpAmp"
  operator_symbol: "&&"
  level: And
}

data binary_op_eqeq: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "EqEq"
  operator_symbol: "=="
  level: Comparison
}

data binary_op_noteq: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "NotEq"
  operator_symbol: "!="
  level: Comparison
}

data binary_op_lt: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "Lt"
  operator_symbol: "<"
  level: Comparison
}

data binary_op_le: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "Le"
  operator_symbol: "<="
  level: Comparison
}

data binary_op_gt: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "Gt"
  operator_symbol: ">"
  level: Comparison
}

data binary_op_ge: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "Ge"
  operator_symbol: ">="
  level: Comparison
}

data binary_op_plus: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "Plus"
  operator_symbol: "+"
  level: Additive
}

data binary_op_minus: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "Minus"
  operator_symbol: "-"
  level: Additive
}

data binary_op_star: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "Star"
  operator_symbol: "*"
  level: Multiplicative
}

data binary_op_slash: BinaryOpRow = {
  token_variant: "Slash"
  operator_symbol: "/"
  level: Multiplicative
}

// --- SG-2c-2: top-level item keyword dispatch (`parse_item` in
// `parse_parser_body.txt`). Each row lists one dedicated keyword
// `TokenKind` variant. **Substrate authority is only `token_variant`**.
// Regen emits the Rust projection `ItemDispatchKind` by taking the unique
// set of `strip_prefix("Kw")` labels from all rows (`KwLet` → `Let`) — there
// is **no** separate `ItemDispatchKind` coproduct authored here (M7 / one
// domain, one authority in `parse_tables.dag`).
//
// Dispatch classification for top-level item forms — discriminant-only
// projection keyed by authoritative lexer tokens (join `tokenize.dag`).
//
// Dissolution classification: **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** per
// `docs/modeling-discipline.md` §4. Same structural situation as
// `BinaryOpLevel`: each emitted enum variant is a parser entry coordinate, not a
// distinct payload algebra; full dissolution rides SG-2c proper (blocked
// on recursive list-body emission over `List<Token>`).
//
// Dissolution ledger (4-pattern check):
// - **Pattern 1 (fact placement)**: fails. Dispatch keys are coordinate keys for
//   `parse_*_item` entry points, not relocatable facts.
// - **Pattern 2 (variant-is-data)**: **passes**: substrate rows are
//   `token_variant` only; the Rust `ItemDispatchKind` enum is a pure projection
//   over those strings, not a second `.dag` coproduct.
// - **Pattern 3 (algebraic form)**: fails. No shared algebra across item forms.
// - **Pattern 4 (dimensional)**: fails / not applicable (cardinality comes only from
//   how many `TopLevelItemKwRow` facts exist, not from a substrate enum type).
//
// **M7 note:** there is **no** `type ItemDispatchKind` in `parse_tables.dag` — only
// `TopLevelItemKwRow` rows. Rust `ItemDispatchKind` is regen-only (unique `Kw`-strip
// labels); not a second authored closed set in substrate.
//
// **Named trigger (YELLOW):** dissolve with SG-2c proper when
// `parse_parser_body.txt` ports to `.dag` list-body recursion.

// Authored fact: which `TokenKind` keyword opens a top-level item (dispatch
// label for Rust is `token_variant.strip_prefix("Kw")`, validated at regen).
//
// **M7 / INVARIANTS (single authority, consumed).** Not a shadow table: regen
// (`regen_parse_tables_emit::collect_top_level_item_kw_rows` → `emit_module`)
// validates each row against `tokenize.dag` and emits
// `parse_tables_generated.rs` (`ItemDispatchKind` + `top_level_item_dispatch`; enum is projection-only).
// The live parser calls `top_level_item_dispatch` from `parse_item`
// (`parse_parser_body.txt`, spliced into `parse_generated.rs`). Ratchet:
// `sg2c1_parse_tables_authority_test` + checked-in generated module snapshot.
type TopLevelItemKwRow {
  token_variant: String
}

// Each row below feeds `collect_top_level_item_kw_rows` → emitted
// `parse_tables_generated.rs::top_level_item_dispatch`; `parse_item` calls that
// helper instead of matching `TokenKind::Kw*` — not a duplicate dispatch table.

data top_level_kw_let: TopLevelItemKwRow = {
  token_variant: "KwLet"
}

data top_level_kw_fn: TopLevelItemKwRow = {
  token_variant: "KwFn"
}

data top_level_kw_type: TopLevelItemKwRow = {
  token_variant: "KwType"
}

data top_level_kw_module: TopLevelItemKwRow = {
  token_variant: "KwModule"
}

data top_level_kw_import: TopLevelItemKwRow = {
  token_variant: "KwImport"
}

data top_level_kw_data: TopLevelItemKwRow = {
  token_variant: "KwData"
}

// --- SG-2c-5: keyword-token aliases that the parser accepts as bare
// identifier spellings in label/name positions. Today this is the
// single `KwType -> "type"` carveout used by both record-field labels
// and sum-variant names. The parser consumes the generated
// `soft_keyword_ident_spelling` projection rather than duplicating the
// `TokenKind::KwType => "type"` match at each call site.
//
// Dissolution classification: **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)**. Same shape as
// `TopLevelItemKwRow`: substrate rows author only `token_variant`; the
// Rust string spelling is a projection (`Kw` prefix stripped and
// lowercased), not a second `.dag` field. Full dissolution rides
// SG-2c proper when parser control flow ports out of
// `parse_parser_body.txt`.
type SoftKeywordIdentRow {
  token_variant: String
}

data soft_keyword_ident_type: SoftKeywordIdentRow = {
  token_variant: "KwType"
}

// --- SG-2c-4: bracket opener / closer membership table. Parser helpers
// that skip or scan token spans while tracking paren/brace/bracket depth
// (`skip_where_clause`, `rhs_is_sum` in `parse_parser_body.txt`) dispatch
// on exactly this three-pair set. Authored here once and consumed via
// the generated `bracket_role` projection; the two duplicated inline
// `TokenKind::L{Paren,Brace,Bracket}` / `TokenKind::R{Paren,Brace,Bracket}`
// match blocks collapse to one structural lookup.
//
// Dissolution classification: **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** per
// `docs/modeling-discipline.md` §4. Same structural situation as the
// other SG-2c tables: each emitted `BracketRole` variant is a
// parser-dispatch coordinate, not a distinct payload algebra; full
// dissolution rides SG-2c proper (blocked on recursive list-body
// emission over `List<Token>`).
//
// Dissolution ledger (4-pattern check):
// - **Pattern 1 (fact placement)**: fails. Role is a coordinate key for
//   depth-tracking control flow, not a relocatable payload.
// - **Pattern 2 (variant-is-data)**: **passes**: substrate rows are
//   `token_variant` only; the Rust `BracketRole` enum is a pure
//   projection derived from the `L`/`R` prefix at regen time, not a
//   second `.dag` coproduct and not a separately authored field (same
//   one-authority shape as `TopLevelItemKwRow` → `ItemDispatchKind`).
// - **Pattern 3 (algebraic form)**: fails. Openers and closers are
//   not elements of a shared computed algebra at this level; bracket
//   pairing is enforced by the grammar structurally, not here.
// - **Pattern 4 (dimensional)**: fails. Not a numeric ordering.
//
// **Named trigger (YELLOW):** dissolve with SG-2c proper when
// `parse_parser_body.txt` ports to `.dag` list-body recursion and the
// depth-tracking helpers become structural traversals rather than
// token-index scans.

// One row per bracketing `TokenKind` variant. Keyed on the textual
// variant name (same convention as `BinaryOpRow` / `TopLevelItemKwRow`)
// and cross-validated against `tokenize.dag::TokenKind` at regen.
//
// **M7 / INVARIANTS (single authority).** `token_variant` is the only
// authored field; `BracketRole` is emitted by regen as a pure projection
// over the `L`/`R` prefix of each row's `token_variant` — not authored
// here as a separate field or as a `.dag` coproduct. Mirrors
// `TopLevelItemKwRow` → `ItemDispatchKind` (dispatch label derived via
// `strip_prefix("Kw")`): one authored fact, role follows structurally.
type BracketRow {
  token_variant: String
}

data bracket_lparen: BracketRow = {
  token_variant: "LParen"
}

data bracket_lbrace: BracketRow = {
  token_variant: "LBrace"
}

data bracket_lbracket: BracketRow = {
  token_variant: "LBracket"
}

data bracket_rparen: BracketRow = {
  token_variant: "RParen"
}

data bracket_rbrace: BracketRow = {
  token_variant: "RBrace"
}

data bracket_rbracket: BracketRow = {
  token_variant: "RBracket"
}

// --- SG-2c-6: `parse_primary` prefix opener dispatch. Before the
// post-bump atomic match (`IntLit`, booleans, `StringLit`, `|`, ident),
// `parse_primary` dispatches on exactly this closed set of peek tokens:
// `if`, `match`, `{`, `[` → dedicated parsers. Authored here once;
// `PrimaryPrefixDispatch` is regen-only (projection over `token_variant`
// rows — same M7 shape as `TopLevelItemKwRow` → `ItemDispatchKind`).
//
// Dissolution classification: **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** per
// `docs/modeling-discipline.md` §4. Same structural situation as the
// other SG-2c tables: each emitted `PrimaryPrefixDispatch` variant is a
// parser entry coordinate for a dedicated `parse_*` arm, not a distinct
// payload algebra; full dissolution rides SG-2c proper (blocked on
// recursive list-body emission over `List<Token>`).
//
// Dissolution ledger (4-pattern check):
// - **Pattern 1 (fact placement)**: fails. Prefix keys are coordinate keys
//   for `parse_if` / `parse_match` / `parse_record_literal` /
//   `parse_list_literal` entry points, not relocatable facts.
// - **Pattern 2 (variant-is-data)**: **passes**: substrate rows are
//   `token_variant` only; the Rust `PrimaryPrefixDispatch` enum is a pure
//   projection at regen time, not a second `.dag` coproduct.
// - **Pattern 3 (algebraic form)**: fails. No shared algebra across these
//   four distinct primary forms at this token-dispatch layer.
// - **Pattern 4 (dimensional)**: fails. Not a numeric ordering.
//
// **Named trigger (YELLOW):** dissolve with SG-2c proper when
// `parse_parser_body.txt` ports to `.dag` list-body recursion over
// `List<Token>` (substrate capability per `src/v3/std/list.dag:13-15`) and
// `parse_primary` prefix openers become structural dispatch in the ported
// parse module — this `PrimaryPrefixRow` table folds into that parse
// authority instead of a separate regen-only Rust host shim.
//
// **M7 note:** no `type PrimaryPrefixDispatch` in substrate — only
// `PrimaryPrefixRow { token_variant }`; Rust enum labels derive at regen
// (`Kw*` → `strip_prefix("Kw")`; `LBrace` → `Record`; `LBracket` → `List`).

type PrimaryPrefixRow {
  token_variant: String
}

data primary_prefix_kw_if: PrimaryPrefixRow = {
  token_variant: "KwIf"
}

data primary_prefix_kw_match: PrimaryPrefixRow = {
  token_variant: "KwMatch"
}

data primary_prefix_lbrace: PrimaryPrefixRow = {
  token_variant: "LBrace"
}

data primary_prefix_lbracket: PrimaryPrefixRow = {
  token_variant: "LBracket"
}

// --- SG-2c-7: `parse_primary` atomic tail (after prefix pass). The bump that
// follows a non-prefix `peek` must be one of: integer literal, boolean
// keyword literals, string, `Pipe` (single `|`, not `PipeArrow` / `|>`) for
// lambda syntax, or identifier — the
// closed set that the parser accepts as a primary expression *atom*. Authored
// here once; `PrimaryAtomClass` and `primary_atom_class` are regen-only
// (projection over `token_variant` rows, same M7 shape as
// `PrimaryPrefixRow` → `PrimaryPrefixDispatch`).
//
// **Cluster boundary (SG-2c wave).** This table pairs with SG-2c-6: both are
// `parse_primary`-local dispatch; together they form one “parser dispatch
// family” extraction (prefix openers + atomic forms) under a single
// `parse_tables` authority surface.
//
// Dissolution classification: **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)**. Same as other
// `parse_tables` row families. Full dissolution rides SG-2c proper (blocked
// on recursive `List<Token>` list-body emission).
type PrimaryAtomRow {
  token_variant: String
}

// Dispatch labels (Rust `PrimaryAtomClass` variants) derive at regen: see
// `primary_atom_class_label_from_token_variant` in `regen_parse_tables_emit.rs`
// (closed allowlist: `IntLit` → `IntLiteral`, `Kw{True,False}` → `{True,False}`,
// `StringLit` → `String`, `Pipe` → `Pipe`, `Ident` → `Ident`).

data primary_atom_int_lit: PrimaryAtomRow = {
  token_variant: "IntLit"
}

data primary_atom_kw_true: PrimaryAtomRow = {
  token_variant: "KwTrue"
}

data primary_atom_kw_false: PrimaryAtomRow = {
  token_variant: "KwFalse"
}

data primary_atom_string_lit: PrimaryAtomRow = {
  token_variant: "StringLit"
}

data primary_atom_pipe: PrimaryAtomRow = {
  token_variant: "Pipe"
}

data primary_atom_ident: PrimaryAtomRow = {
  token_variant: "Ident"
}
